# P2.8 (cross-platform reproducibility): every file is checked out EXACTLY as committed, on every OS. Without this a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true on GitHub runners) turned LF text into CRLF, and the deployment artefact built
# from it differed from the Linux one (different sha256, +48 KB). The repository bytes are the build input.
* -text
# Generated artefacts are collapsed in GitHub diffs so review focuses on
# src/ → server/ → scripts/ → schemas/ → tests/ (P0.15.4).
public/app-preview/** linguist-generated=true
dist-rc/** linguist-generated=true
dist-standalone/** linguist-generated=true
reports/** linguist-generated=true
review-packets/** linguist-generated=true
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
